course: dictionary
lesson: 10832
title: One word, two jobs: vent
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Vent can be a thing or an action. As a noun, a vent is a small opening that lets air, smoke, steam or gas go in or out, like an air vent in a room. As a verb, to vent means to let your feelings out, especially anger.
explain: The context shows you which meaning is right. «Vent water can be hotter than three hundred degrees, but it does not boil» is about hot water coming out of the sea floor, so vent is an opening. «Shouting at the TV is venting, letting out frustration» is about feelings, so vent is an action.
explain: Look at the words stuck to vent, too. Phrases like «air vent», «give vent to» and «hydrothermal vent» give you clues. Then test your meaning in the sentence: if "opening" fits, it is the noun; if "let out" fits, it is the verb.
fact: Vent (noun) means a small opening that lets air, smoke, steam or gas go in or out.
fact: Vent (verb) means to let out feelings, especially anger, by talking, shouting or crying.
fact: A volcanic vent is the opening where melted rock, gas and ash escape from inside the Earth.
fact: Hydrothermal vents are openings on the ocean floor that let out hot water, and «Vent water can be hotter than three hundred degrees, but it does not boil because of the huge pressure of the deep sea.»
exercise: «Keep vents clear, especially on gas heaters, for safety.» What is a vent here? | A kind of heater | *A small opening that lets gas or air out | A slit in a coat | A feeling of anger
exercise: Shouting at the TV is «venting». What is venting? | *Letting frustration out | Turning the TV off | Making the TV louder
exercise: «A volcano is an opening in the crust where melted rock, gas and ash escape.» Which word in the sentence means come out? | melted | *escape | volcano | crust
test: «Before vents were found in 1977, scientists thought all life on Earth depended on sunlight.» What did scientists think life depended on before vents were found? | Ocean floors | Water | *Sunlight | Volcanoes
test: In «She vented about her day», what does vented mean? | *Let her feelings out by talking | Opened a door for some air | Broke a window | Gave a long speech about the weather
exam: Which statement about vent is true? | A vent is always a volcano | A vent is only a kind of coat | Vent only ever means anger | *A vent can be an opening, or a way of letting feelings out
